Feature: Customer dropdown # features/home_page.feature:1
  As a user opening the home page
  I want to see a customer dropdown
  So that I can select a customer
  Scenario: Default option shows "Select Customer"          # features/home_page.feature:6
    Given the app is running                                # steps/home_steps.py:81
    When I open the home page                               # steps/home_steps.py:91
    Then the customer dropdown default is "Select Customer" # steps/home_steps.py:97

  Scenario: Customer dropdown is rendered and functional    # features/home_page.feature:10
    Given I am on the home page                             # steps/home_steps.py:85
    When I click the customer dropdown                      # steps/home_steps.py:144
    Then the dropdown should be visible and contain options # steps/home_steps.py:152

  @api
  Scenario: Customer dropdown is populated from API and selection persists  # features/home_page.feature:16
    Given I am on the home page                                             # steps/home_steps.py:85
    When I wait for the customer dropdown to be populated from the API      # steps/home_steps.py:109
    And I select the first available customer                               # steps/home_steps.py:114
    Then the selected customer remains selected in the dropdown             # steps/home_steps.py:136

Feature: Primary navigation from Home # features/navigation.feature:1
  As a user
  I want to move between core pages from the Home page
  So that I can complete key flows
  Background:   # features/navigation.feature:6

  Scenario: Navigate from Home to Purchase Rings to Manage Orders to About Us  # features/navigation.feature:10
    Given the app is running                                                   # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I open the home page                                                   # steps/navigation_steps.py:65
    When I navigate to "Purchase Rings"                                        # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then I should be on the "Purchase Rings" page                              # steps/navigation_steps.py:100
    When I navigate to "Manage Orders"                                         # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then I should be on the "Manage Orders" page                               # steps/navigation_steps.py:100
    When I navigate to "About Us"                                              # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then I should be on the "About Us" page                                    # steps/navigation_steps.py:100

Feature: Purchase Rings page # features/purchase_rings.feature:1
  As a user on the Purchase Rings page
  I want to add rings to my cart
  So that I can purchase them
  Background:   # features/purchase_rings.feature:6

  @api
  Scenario: Add to cart shows a confirmation alert                          # features/purchase_rings.feature:12
    Given the app is running                                                # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I am on the home page                                               # steps/home_steps.py:85
    And I select the first customer from the dropdown                       # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:65
    And I navigate to "Purchase Rings"                                      # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Given the purchase rings page has loaded                                # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:92
    When I click the Add to Cart button on the first ring                   # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:125
    Then an alert should appear with the message "Added 1 ring(s) to cart!" # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:134

  Scenario: Configure all ring options and verify the cart item matches        # features/purchase_rings.feature:17
    Given the app is running                                                   # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I am on the home page                                                  # steps/home_steps.py:85
    And I select the first customer from the dropdown                          # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:65
    And I navigate to "Purchase Rings"                                         # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Given the purchase rings page has loaded                                   # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:92
    When I select the second option in the material dropdown on the first ring # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:100
    And I select the second option in the width dropdown on the first ring     # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:106
    And I select the second option in the stone dropdown on the first ring     # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:112
    And I set the quantity to 2 on the first ring                              # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:118
    And I click the Add to Cart button on the first ring                       # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:125
    Then an alert should appear with the message "Added 2 ring(s) to cart!"    # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:134
    When I navigate to "Cart"                                                  # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then the cart should contain at least 1 item                               # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:145
    And the first cart item should show quantity 2                             # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:155
    And the first cart item should show the selected material value            # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:166
    And the first cart item should show the selected stone value               # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:178

